:53:58.081Z","effort":"medium","perTurnEffort":"medium","userType":"external","entrypoint":"claude-desktop","cwd":"/Users/nsviridenko/ws/sloprail/harness-mocks/.claude/worktrees/agent-a5206b5b2ad4bea59","sessionId":"f103aecd-8ff6-40a5-ad21-f5bd02338666","version":"2.1.286","gitBranch":"worktree-agent-a513ce3b392834fe0"}
{"parentUuid":"8f7427d6-12a0-4294-b61f-3d50817fc30c","isSidechain":true,"promptId":"6b8557a2-9430-4f17-946a-1ea07dab5643","agentId":"a5206b5b2ad4bea59","type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_013owzV6ECTFTdCkBdtBh7U1","type":"tool_result","content":"29:### Foreground vs background\n35:| **Foreground** | Blocks until the subagent completes. Returns the result immediately. | Sequential tasks where you need the output. |\n36:| **Background** | Returns immediately. The subagent works independently.               | Long-running tasks or parallel workstreams. |\n129:| `is_background` | boolean | No       | `false`               | If `true`, the subagent runs in the background without blocking the parent.                                                          |\n298:Background subagents write their state as they run. You can resume a subagent after it completes to continue the conversation with preserved context.\n463:Background subagents write output to `~/.cursor/subagents/`. The parent agent can read these files to check progress.\n---\n5:ChatGPT Work and Codex can run subagent workflows by spawning specialized\n66:delegation. When the background-agent UI is available, active subagents appear\n81:For background, see the Chroma writeup on [context rot](https://research.trychroma.com/context-rot).\n126:\"spawn two agents,\" \"delegate this work in parallel,\" or \"use one agent per\n131:should wait for all agents before continuing, and what summary or output to\n135:Review this branch with parallel subagents. Spawn one subagent for security risks, one for test gaps, and one for maintainability. Wait for all three, then summarize the findings by category with file references.\n159:spawn request or an `[agents]` default selects a model without an\n198:ChatGPT or Codex handles orchestration across agents, including spawning new\n199:subagents, routing follow-up instructions, waiting for results, and closing\n202:When many agents are running, Codex waits until all requested results are\n207:At most intelligence levels, ChatGPT spawns agents after a direct request. With\n214:Current local Codex releases spawn agents after a direct request or applicable\n222:I would like to review the following points on the current PR (this branch vs main). Spawn one agent per point, wait for all of them, and summarize the result for each point.\n272:- When the background-agent panel is available, expand it to inspect status,\n314:Codex also reapplies the parent turn's live runtime overrides when it spawns a\n345:layers for spawned sessions, so custom agents can override the same settings as\n357:from an explicit spawn value, then the corresponding `[agents]` default, then\n358:the parent's value. If an explicit spawn request or an `[agents]` default\n374:| `agents.max_concurrent_threads_per_session` | number  |    No    | Cap concurrently open spawned-agent threads, excluding the primary. |\n375:| `agents.default_subagent_model`             | string  |    No    | Set the default model for spawned agents.                           |","is_error":false}]},"uuid":"9f6d8614-3619-4f04-ad57-ed2f69c1370c","timestamp":"2026-10-03T14:53:58.613Z","sourceToolAssistantUUID":"8f7427d6-12a0-4294-b61f-3d50817fc30c","userType":"external","entrypoint":"claude-desktop","cwd":"/Users/nsviridenko/ws/sloprail/harness-mocks/.claude/worktrees/agent-a5206b5b2ad4bea59","sessionId":"f103aecd-8ff6-40a5-ad21-f5bd02338666","version":"2.1.286","gitBranch":"worktree-agent-a513ce3b392834fe0"}
