{"parentUuid":"462e8523-df1b-4ae6-9d53-128ac3a24ed0","isSidechain":true,"promptId":"0e75e1c2-9f84-43c4-8006-cccad7102c77","agentId":"a5206b5b2ad4bea59","type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_011CeCBLExEbgkUAXawQPJpy","type":"tool_result","content":"the following rules refused this work:\n  - capability-once: cursor-mock/internal/runner/background_agent.go (launchTask) is marked `// sr:provides background-agent/cursor`, but spec/capabilities/background-agent.yaml still has `cursor: pending`, and the Decision says adapter code is marked sr:provides and 'exists exactly for the supported cells; a `pending` or unsupported cell has none' — either turn that cell into a supported one with docs and runs (and sr:proves tests), or do not mark and ship that adapter code for a pending cell. (file-guard \"adr-conformance\")\n  - Capabilities not implemented, adapted or proven (adr/capability-once):\n- cursor-mock/internal/runner/background_agent.go: sr:provides background-agent/cursor, but 'background-agent' has no supported cell for 'cursor' ({docs, runs}); a pending or unsupported cell is not coverage (file-guard \"capability-covered\")\n  - Cursor: the statement says every lifecycle hook receives the working directory, but Cursor's common schema (cursor.com/docs/hooks#common-schema) lists only `workspace_roots`, not `cwd`; its cited runs show `cwd` only on tool/shell events (9 of 27 payloads in tool-failure, none on sessionStart or afterAgentThought) and `transcript_path` is null throughout, and no deviation records this.\n  - codex: the statement says exit 2 uses the hook stderr as the message only when the hook gave no other reason, but codex-mock/snapshots/runs/hook-exit-json (echo h: JSON deny reason \"the JSON reason wins\" with stderr \"the stderr loses\" on exit 2) shows the real harness blocking with the stderr text (\"Command blocked by PreToolUse hook: the stderr loses\"), so the codex cell needs a deviation for it.\n  - Cursor: the statement's 'whatever it printed is discarded' part is neither stated by the doc (only 'timeout | Execution timeout in seconds') nor shown by cursor-mock/snapshots/runs/hook-timeout, because setup/slow.sh prints its deny only after `sleep 5`, so it never prints anything before the 1s timeout kills it; the run shows the grandchild killed and the event carrying on, but not discarded output, and the cell lists no deviation for it (Codex's run does show this, since its hook prints the deny before the timeout).\n  - Codex is cited as supporting 'how long the call took', but its PostToolUse docs table lists only turn_id, tool_name, tool_use_id, tool_input and tool_response (no duration), and the recorded payloads in codex-mock/snapshots/runs/stops and posttool-block carry no duration field; the codex provider has no deviation for it (only cursor does), so the statement claims a part Codex neither documents nor shows.\n  - The statement part \"Whatever the hook prints is not recorded in the transcript\" is neither documented nor shown for codex (doc says only \"advisory, so their output won't steer Codex\"; the run hook.sh prints nothing to stdout, it only appends to HOOK_LOG) nor for cursor (doc says \"The response is logged but not used\"; the pretool-refusal hook.sh prints nothing for sessionEnd), and it is not listed as a deviation.\n  - Codex is listed as supported with no deviations, but the statement says the Stop payload carries the background tasks still running; the Codex Stop doc table lists only turn_id, stop_hook_active and last_assistant_message, and the cited stops run's Stop payloads show no background-tasks field. Add this part as a Codex deviation, or ground it with a run.\n  - Codex: the statement's part \"It also fires for a background-task notification handed to the agent\" is not stated in the #userpromptsubmit doc section (it only says the hook receives \"User prompt that's about to be sent\"), is not shown by the cited runs hook-exit-codes or prompt-blocked (their UserPromptSubmit payloads only carry the user's typed prompt), and is not listed as a codex deviation; \"cannot rewrite\" is likewise stated by neither doc nor run.\n  - cursor: the recorded tool-failure run (shell command printing only to stderr, `sh -c 'echo OOPS >&2; exit 3'`, failure message \"OOPS\") is not driven by any test marked sr:proves bash-tool-result/cursor; TestAShellCommandExitingNonZeroIsAFailureResultWithItsOutputOrExitCode replays only shell-exit-status (no stderr-only case), and the tool-failure replay is claimed for file-tools/cursor, so the stderr-only variant has no explicit assertion.\n  - hook-command-handler/codex: TestCommandHookReadsThePayloadOnStdinInTheSessionDirectory only runs hooks with the session started at the repo root and a pwd/pipe command line, so it cannot tell 'session cwd' (hooks#config-shape: 'Commands run with the session cwd as their working directory', 'Codex may be started from a subdirectory') from the git root or project root; it never starts a session in a subdirectory, and none of the codex tests exercises the recorded hook form (command substitution '\"$(git rev-parse --show-toplevel)\"/hook.sh') as a hook-command-handler assertion. Add a test with the session cwd in a subdirectory (hook pwd == that subdirectory) and a $(...) command line.\n  - hook-matcher-filter/cursor: the doc states that an empty-string matcher matches everything and that afterShellExecution is matched on the command text (and postToolUseFailure on the tool name), but the only test file (cursor-mock/e2e/001_hooks/matcher_timeout_test.go) and the hook-matchers recording use only '*' and an omitted matcher, so no test covers an empty matcher, an afterShellExecution matcher, or a postToolUseFailure matcher. Related codex gap: the doc says to omit matcher entirely to match everything, but no test uses a hook with the matcher omitted (only '*' and ''). The codex tests otherwise match the recording: session-startup ran and resume did not, pre-star, pre-bash and pre-empty ran while pre-edit-write and pre-nomatch did not, the UserPromptSubmit and Stop matchers were ignored, and the apply_patch aliases are covered by the unit test.\n  - noninteractive-run/codex: all three recorded streams (stops, hook-exit-codes, prompt-blocked) carry two item.completed events with subtype error right after thread.started, and stops has several agent_message items, some before the command_execution. The tests assert stream shape through streamShape(), which silently drops every error and agent_message item, so none of these is checked. The deviation covers only a stream-level error event, not these items. The doc also says progress streams to stderr while only the final message goes to stdout, but TestExecWithoutJSONPrintsOnlyTheFinalMessage asserts stdout only and no test checks stderr.\n  - posttooluse-payload/codex: TestPostToolUsePayloadCarriesInputAndResponse covers only one successful `echo FINE` and never checks that PostToolUse still fires (with tool_response) for a Bash command that exits non-zero, which the doc states, or that it does not fire for the PreToolUse-denied or exit-2-blocked calls in runs/stops. posttool-block, where PostToolUse fires twice for POSTBLOCK, is never replayed. posttooluse-payload/cursor: the proving test replays only file-tools and never asserts that postToolUse is absent (postToolUseFailure instead) for the failed and refused calls recorded in tool-failure and pretool-refusal. It also checks only NotEmpty for tool_output instead of the recorded values, such as the Shell tool_output {\"output\":\"FINE\n  - session-end-hook/codex: the Codex doc (hooks#sessionend) says 'SessionEnd hooks always run synchronously, even when async is true', but no codex-mock test configures an async SessionEnd hook and checks it runs to completion before the run exits (no 'async' appears in codex-mock/e2e) and no recorded run shows it; the other checklist items (reason 'other', fires last, no model/permission_mode, output not recorded, failing hook is advisory) and the cursor subject (reason/final_status 'completed', output not in transcript, deviation declared) are covered.\n  - session-start-hook/cursor: the doc (cursor hooks#sessionStart) says session creation is not blocked even when the hook returns `continue: false`, but cursor-mock/e2e/001_hooks/session_start_test.go only tries exit 2, so no test covers that doc-stated variant. session-start-hook/codex: the doc lists source `clear` as a fourth start variant, but the codex deviation covers only resume, fork and compact, and no test or deviation addresses `clear`.\n  - TestStopPayloadCarriesLastMessageAndContinuing asserts last_assistant_message only on the first Stop (\"DONE\"). The recording shows the continuation Stops carry the new message (\"DONE2\"), with stop_hook_active true on both the second and third Stop, so a mock that repeated the stale first message would still pass. The test also never checks the doc-stated turn_id field, which is the same on every Stop in the run, and it never reaches a third Stop. The stop-block-continuation test counts three Stop events but pins no payload fields.\n  - The only test marked sr:proves user-prompt-submit-hook/codex (TestUserPromptSubmitAddsContextOrRefuses) leaves doc and run items unchecked. (1) The doc's JSON block shape (decision:block) and JSON hookSpecificOutput.additionalContext are not exercised under this capability; the JSON-block test is marked hook-exit-code-semantics instead. (2) The refusal case never drives the mock with an exit-2 hook; it only replays the prompt-blocked recording and asserts the stream shape [thread.started, turn.started, turn.completed], without checking that the agent never ran or that the hook payload (prompt, permission_mode=bypassPermissions) matches the sample. (3) Only the prompt field of the UserPromptSubmit payload is asserted, not session_id, hook_event_name or permission_mode shown in the runs. (4) The doc says matcher is not used for UserPromptSubmit, and no test covers that.\n\n[exited with code 0]","is_error":false}]},"uuid":"534ff8a0-ea6c-42cf-a60f-d43c4f51ba43","timestamp":"2026-10-03T15:12:27.544Z","sourceToolAssistantUUID":"462e8523-df1b-4ae6-9d53-128ac3a24ed0","userType":"external","entrypoint":"claude-desktop","cwd":"/Users/nsviridenko/ws/sloprail/harness-mocks/.claude/worktrees/agent-a5206b5b2ad4bea59","sessionId":"f103aecd-8ff6-40a5-ad21-f5bd02338666","version":"2.1.286","gitBranch":"worktree-agent-a513ce3b392834fe0"}
