{"parentUuid":"2ed0f279-6de3-48e2-8093-669a726ba11d","isSidechain":true,"promptId":"0e75e1c2-9f84-43c4-8006-cccad7102c77","agentId":"a5206b5b2ad4bea59","type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_01RJ2o6NgeP26Uag7g9yj794","type":"tool_result","content":"the following rules refused this work:\n  - The statement covers the working directory, and every recorded tool-hook payload carries \"cwd\":\"\" (preToolUse, beforeShellExecution, postToolUseFailure), but no test asserts the cwd field. TestEveryHookPayloadNamesTheSessionTheTranscriptAndTheWorkspace checks session_id, conversation_id, workspace_roots and transcript_path only, and it also does not check the user_email:null, cursor_version or generation_id fields the docs list as common. The sub-agent part is covered by the modeled-surface deviation.\n  - The headless doc (#how-it-works, lines 9-27) says print mode without --force/--yolo only proposes changes and does not modify files, while with --force it applies them. The mock only accepts and ignores --force/--yolo (cursor-mock/root.go:42-43, 'accepted, ignored'). The modeled-surface deviation does not declare this, and no test runs with and without --force to check what happens to file changes. Add a test and a recorded run for it, or declare a deviation.\n  - TestAfterAToolSucceedsTheHookGetsItsInputItsOutputAndHowLongItTook requires every postToolUse payload to carry a float64 `duration`, but no recorded postToolUse in file-tools or tool-failure has that field (e.g. file-tools line 6 has only tool_name, tool_input, tool_output, session_id, hook_event_name), so the test pins a value the recordings contradict. The Shell postToolUse (tool-failure line 39, tool_output {\"output\":\"FINE\n  - No test refuses a non-shell tool: the docs say preToolUse fires for all tool types (Shell, Read, Write, ...) and the mock fires it for Read/Write file tools (hooks.PreToolUse with tool name Read/Write), but every refusal test (pretool_test.go, custom_