{"parentUuid":"7ac945e8-6ed2-4f6b-a1d0-094f5f4b07aa","isSidechain":true,"promptId":"0e75e1c2-9f84-43c4-8006-cccad7102c77","agentId":"a5206b5b2ad4bea59","type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_01U8rgh8NW6mPyhLbFKusEB3","type":"tool_result","content":"1:# Using Headless CLI\n5:## How it works\n9:### File modification in scripts\n14:# Enable file modifications in print mode\n17:# Without --force, changes are only proposed, not applied\n20:# Batch processing with actual file changes\n29:## Setup\n34:# Install Cursor CLI (macOS, Linux, WSL)\n37:# Install Cursor CLI (Windows PowerShell)\n40:# Set API key for scripts\n45:## Example scripts\n49:### Searching the codebase\n54:#!/bin/bash\n55:# Simple codebase question - uses text format by default\n60:### Automated code review\n65:#!/bin/bash\n66:# simple-code-review.sh - Basic code review script\n70:# Review recent changes\n88:### Real-time progress tracking\n93:#!/bin/bash\n94:# stream-progress.sh - Track progress in real-time\n98:# Track progress in real-time\n168:## Working with images\n172:### Including file paths in prompts\n177:# Analyze an image\n180:# Process multiple media files\n183:# Combine file paths with text instructions\n187:### How it works\n196:### Example: Image analysis script\n199:#!/bin/bash\n200:# analyze-image.sh - Analyze images using the headless CLI\n209:### Example: Batch media processing\n212:#!/bin/bash\n213:# process-media.sh - Process multiple media files\n229:## Sitemap\n13:- Control subagent (Task tool) execution\n28:- `subagentStart` / `subagentStop` - Subagent (Task tool) lifecycle\n69:| `subagentStart`        | Yes       |\n70:| `subagentStop`         | Yes       |\n194:- Exit code `0` - Hook succeeded, use the JSON output. For permission hooks (`beforeShellExecution`, `beforeMCPExecution`, `beforeReadFile`, `beforeTabFileRead`, `subagentStart`, `preToolUse`), invalid JSON or a response that doesn't match the hook's schema blocks the action.\n676:    \"subagentStart\": [{ \"command\": \"./hooks/validate-subagent.sh\" }],\n677:    \"subagentStop\": [{ \"command\": \"./hooks/audit-subagent.sh\" }],\n691:The Agent hooks (`sessionStart`, `sessionEnd`, `preToolUse`, `postToolUse`, `postToolUseFailure`, `subagentStart`, `subagentStop`, `beforeShellExecution`, `afterShellExecution`, `beforeMCPExecution`, `afterMCPExecution`, `beforeReadFile`, `afterFileEdit`, `beforeSubmitPrompt`, `preCompact`, `stop`, `afterAgentResponse`, `afterAgentThought`) apply to Cmd+K and Agent Chat operations. The Tab hooks (`beforeTabFileRead`, `afterTabFileEdit`) apply specifically to inline Tab completions. The app lifecycle hook (`workspaceOpen`) fires when a workspace opens and on workspace folder changes, independent of any agent session.\n706:| `loop_limit` | number \\| null            | `5`              | Per-script loop limit for stop/subagentStop hooks. `null` means no limit. Default is `5` for Cursor hooks, `null` for Claude Code hooks.                                                                                                                 |\n724:    \"subagentStart\": [","is_error":false}]},"uuid":"91402eb8-309e-4c4c-abe3-f821328762d1","timestamp":"2026-10-03T16:30:24.827Z","sourceToolAssistantUUID":"7ac945e8-6ed2-4f6b-a1d0-094f5f4b07aa","userType":"external","entrypoint":"claude-desktop","cwd":"/Users/nsviridenko/ws/sloprail/harness-mocks/.claude/worktrees/agent-a5206b5b2ad4bea59","sessionId":"f103aecd-8ff6-40a5-ad21-f5bd02338666","version":"2.1.286","gitBranch":"worktree-agent-adc1470310079e23b"}
