{"parentUuid":"e0774efc-fe3f-477d-a672-2f736787d010","isSidechain":true,"agentId":"a5206b5b2ad4bea59","attachment":{"type":"edited_text_file","filename":"/Users/nsviridenko/ws/sloprail/harness-mocks/.claude/worktrees/agent-a5206b5b2ad4bea59/cursor-mock/internal/runner/background_wait.go","snippet":"11\tconst followUp = \"Perform any necessary follow-up actions in response to the subagent completion above. If no follow-up work is needed, no further action is required. If you mention an agent or subagent in your response, link it with the `[Name](id)` Don't use generic label such as `[agent]`, `[worker]`, or `[subagent]`. Don't repeat the same confirmation every time.\"\n12\t\n13\t// notification is what a finished background task puts on the stream, and the\n14\t// prompt of the further turn it starts: a sub-agent's end is announced with its\n15\t// prompt as the title and what it said as the detail, and the session, which\n16\t// stays open while one runs (afterTurn), gives the agent a turn to handle it.\n17\t//\n18\t// sr:provides print-waits-for-background-agents/cursor\n19\tfunc (s *session) notification(t *tasks.Task) (frame []byte, turn string) {\n20\t\tif t.Kind != tasks.Agent {\n21\t\t\treturn notificationFrame(s.id, t), notificationPrompt\n22\t\t}\n23\t\tprompt, _ := t.Meta.(string)\n24\t\ttitle := []rune(prompt)\n25\t\tif len(title) > 80 {\n26\t\t\ttitle = title[:80]\n27\t\t}\n28\t\tstatus, detail := \"success\", t.Result\n29\t\tif t.Status() != tasks.Completed {\n30\t\t\tstatus, detail = \"error\", t.Failure\n31\t\t}\n32\t\treturn jsonLine(map[string]any{"},"type":"attachment","uuid":"7b6671c1-de7d-4dd1-8749-c7b4bcc1a4cb","timestamp":"2026-10-03T16:46:33.054Z","rendered":[{"content":"<system-reminder>\nNote: /Users/nsviridenko/ws/sloprail/harness-mocks/.claude/worktrees/agent-a5206b5b2ad4bea59/cursor-mock/internal/runner/background_wait.go changed on disk since you last read it. That's usually deliberate, so take it as the current state rather than reverting it; if the change looks wrong, say so rather than undoing it yourself — otherwise no need to call it out. Here are the relevant changes (shown with line numbers):\n11\tconst followUp = \"Perform any necessary follow-up actions in response to the subagent completion above. If no follow-up work is needed, no further action is required. If you mention an agent or subagent in your response, link it with the `[Name](id)` Don't use generic label such as `[agent]`, `[worker]`, or `[subagent]`. Don't repeat the same confirmation every time.\"\n12\t\n13\t// notification is what a finished background task puts on the stream, and the\n14\t// prompt of the further turn it starts: a sub-agent's end is announced with its\n15\t// prompt as the title and what it said as the detail, and the session, which\n16\t// stays open while one runs (afterTurn), gives the agent a turn to handle it.\n17\t//\n18\t// sr:provides print-waits-for-background-agents/cursor\n19\tfunc (s *session) notification(t *tasks.Task) (frame []byte, turn string) {\n20\t\tif t.Kind != tasks.Agent {\n21\t\t\treturn notificationFrame(s.id, t), notificationPrompt\n22\t\t}\n23\t\tprompt, _ := t.Meta.(string)\n24\t\ttitle := []rune(prompt)\n25\t\tif len(title) > 80 {\n26\t\t\ttitle = title[:80]\n27\t\t}\n28\t\tstatus, detail := \"success\", t.Result\n29\t\tif t.Status() != tasks.Completed {\n30\t\t\tstatus, detail = \"error\", t.Failure\n31\t\t}\n32\t\treturn jsonLine(map[string]any{\n</system-reminder>"}],"renderedRole":"system","userType":"external","entrypoint":"claude-desktop","cwd":"/Users/nsviridenko/ws/sloprail/harness-mocks/.claude/worktrees/agent-a5206b5b2ad4bea59","sessionId":"f103aecd-8ff6-40a5-ad21-f5bd02338666","version":"2.1.286","gitBranch":"worktree-agent-a11c0a040e3cf682b"}
