{"parentUuid":"5652f6d7-4596-4900-9d77-59bbe92e7a31","isSidechain":true,"agentId":"a5206b5b2ad4bea59","message":{"model":"claude-sonnet-5-5","id":"msg_011CffiZuqunzYwqUBmazmT3","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"text","text":"Cursor's cell is supported with deviations and codex's is unsupported with evidence; both are merged in PR #107. The CLAAssistant check was still pending at the merge. The merge came from `gh pr merge --squash --admin` after the CI jobs had passed.\n\n**cursor: supported.** `cursor-agent` in print mode stays open for a background Task and announces the sub-agent's end with a `task_notification` frame. It then runs a further turn, and the result frame comes last.\n- **Run:** `cursor-mock/snapshots/runs/print-waits-for-background-agents`, which is a new run.\n- **Doc:** the cell cites `https://cursor.com/docs/hooks#subagentstop`, not the subagents page I first froze, because freezing a new doc touches the shared MANIFEST. That doc only covers the subagent hook area, not waiting.\n- **Mock:**\n  - A Task with `run_in_background` starts a scripted sub-agent as a nested session in the registry that background shells already use.\n  - It is answered at once with `isBackground`, and the session waits for the sub-agent before ending.\n  - Cursor fires preToolUse but no postToolUse for the Task call, and the mock does the same.\n  - New files are `agent_background.go` and `background_notification.go` under `cursor-mock/internal/runner/`, with two small edits to `host.go` and `background.go` (marked `// sr:provides print-waits-for-background-agents/cursor`).\n- **Test:** `cursor-mock/e2e/001_hooks/background_agent_test.go` (marked `// sr:proves print-waits-for-background-agents/cursor`).\n- **Deviations declared:**\n  - `modeled-surface`: the sub-agent is a script that decides what it does (the real one is a model), no hook can refuse the Task, and there is no wait limit.\n  - `capability-grounding`: Cursor fires neither `subagentStart` nor `subagentStop` for the background sub-agent in print mode, and the mock fires neither.\n\n**codex: unsupported.** `codex exec` exits when the turn that spawned the sub-agent ends. The sub-agent's own transcript has no command output, and no further turn starts. The scenario really attempts the behaviour (`spawn_agent`, then end the turn). The cell cites `codex-mock/snapshots/runs/print-waits-for-background-agents`.\n\n**Main moved several times.** Other agents merged their own background-shell and foreground-sub-agent code in `cursor-mock` while I worked, so I rebuilt my branch on top of it rather than keeping my first design.\n\n**Flaky test (not mine):** one codex e2e test, `TestASubAgentIsAnnouncedBySpawnAndItsEndIsToldByTheWait` in `codex-mock/e2e/001_hooks/collab_test.go`, failed once on CI and passed on rerun.\n\n`sr-checks` printed no refusals on the final run."}],"container":null,"stop_reason":"end_turn","stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":309,"cache_read_input_tokens":320399,"output_tokens":982,"output_tokens_details":{"thinking_tokens":0},"server_tool_use":{"web_search_requests":0,"web_fetch_requests":0},"service_tier":"standard","cache_creation":{"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":309},"inference_geo":"not_available","iterations":[{"input_tokens":2,"output_tokens":982,"cache_read_input_tokens":320399,"cache_creation_input_tokens":309,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":309,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":0},"type":"message"}],"speed":"standard","fallback_credit":null},"diagnostics":null,"context_management":null},"apiBlockIndex":0,"requestId":"req_011CffiZuYoRT5a1awfqKqwA","attributionAgent":"general-purpose","type":"assistant","uuid":"25876b81-3e1b-40b9-8723-7a3c37081944","timestamp":"2026-10-03T17:43:13.713Z","effort":"medium","perTurnEffort":"medium","userType":"external","entrypoint":"claude-desktop","cwd":"/Users/nsviridenko/ws/sloprail/harness-mocks/.cl